1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:10,450
Lesson 22. Susan shares the good news. Bob tells Susan that the village market won't take their cookies anymore.

2
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:17,849
Susan tells Bob that the national cookie company wants to buy out Susan's scrumptious cookies.

3
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:21,049
Dear, I've got some bad news.

4
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:22,769
What's the matter, Bob?

5
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:26,389
The village market won't take any more of our cookies.

6
00:00:26,239 --> 00:00:29,529
Why not? They're selling like hotcakes.

7
00:00:29,879 --> 00:00:35,710
I know, but a lady found a blue hair in her cookie. Now Carol refuses to sell them.

8
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:41,170
Carol is such a dragon lady. We're better off having nothing to do with her.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,710
She's not my cup of tea either, but she was selling lots of cookies.

10
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:50,570
Oh well, that's the way the cookie crumbles. Ha ha, get it?

11
00:00:51,219 --> 00:00:53,229
Susan, this is no laughing matter.

12
00:00:53,079 --> 00:00:57,750
Bob, we don't need the village market anymore. Why not?

13
00:00:58,219 --> 00:01:02,809
The national cookie company called. They want to buy out our business.

14
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:07,990
Susan, this is a dream come true. It looks like we've struck it rich.

15
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:11,090
Yes, soon we'll be rolling in dough.

